    "title": "seed.tbtc.petertodd.net testnet3 DNS seed stuck serving bad addresses",
    "body": "The testnet3 DNS seed ` seed.tbtc.petertodd.net` is stuck serving old and static data, perhaps it has no peers or has otherwise gone stale itself somehow.\n\nFor a number of days I have only seen it return 37 unique ip addresses (24 ipv4, 13 ipv6) in total, with only 1 (ipv6) node actually contactable.\n\n<details>\n<summary>example ipv4 query</summary>\n\n```bash\n❯ dig seed.tbtc.petertodd.net A\n\n; <<>> DiG 9.20.26 <<>> seed.tbtc.petertodd.net A\n;; global options: +cmd\n;; Got answer:\n;; ->>HEADER<<- opcode: QUERY, status: NOERROR, id: 40041\n;; flags: qr rd ra; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 24, AUTHORITY: 0, ADDITIONAL: 1\n\n;; OPT PSEUDOSECTION:\n; EDNS: version: 0, flags:; udp: 1232\n;; QUESTION SECTION:\n;seed.tbtc.petertodd.net.       IN      A\n\n;; ANSWER SECTION:\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       5.188.119.196\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       5.189.162.76\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       13.229.104.97\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       18.162.45.10\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       23.93.101.158\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       34.91.255.249\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       35.207.3.50\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       39.98.193.129\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       51.210.208.202\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       51.210.220.135\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       64.190.113.17\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       71.13.92.62\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       72.211.1.222\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       88.198.91.246\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       99.192.223.18\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       122.248.200.20\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       132.145.213.181\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       138.201.51.42\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       142.44.138.161\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       161.35.211.215\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       178.21.118.96\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       185.180.220.12\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       188.40.164.205\nseed.tbtc.petertodd.net. 3600   IN      A       204.16.241.8\n\n;; Query time: 1040 msec\n;; SERVER: 100.100.100.100#53(100.100.100.100) (UDP)\n;; WHEN: Mon Aug 24 13:21:55 BST 2026\n;; MSG SIZE  rcvd: 436\n```\n\n</details>\n\n@petertodd is this something which you can address? If not then it could be worth removing the testnet3 seed to help bootstrap nodes.",
